{"type":"tool_result","callId":"call_7e1726c43844beef3a8f9267","status":"completed","result":"     1\t---\n     2\ttitle: Deep Research Strategy Template\n     3\tdescription: Runtime template copied to research/ during initialization to track research progress, focus decisions, and outcomes across iterations.\n     4\ttrigger_phrases:\n     5\t  - \"deep research strategy\"\n     6\t  - \"research strategy template\"\n     7\t  - \"research session tracking\"\n     8\t  - \"exhausted research approaches\"\n     9\t  - \"research stop conditions\"\n    10\t  - \"ruled out research directions\"\n    11\timportance_tier: normal\n    12\tcontextType: planning\n    13\tversion: 1.14.0.19\n    14\t---\n    15\t\n    16\t# Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n    17\t\n    18\tRuntime template copied to `{spec_folder}/research/` during initialization. Tracks research progress across iterations.\n    19\t\n    20\t## 1. OVERVIEW\n    21\t\n    22\t### Purpose\n    23\t\n    24\tServes as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep research session. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n    25\t\n    26\t### Usage\n    27\t\n    28\t- **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{spec_folder}/research/deep-research-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Key Questions, Known Context, and Research Boundaries from config and memory context.\n    29\t- **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, writes iteration evidence, and the reducer refreshes What Worked/Failed, answered questions, carried-forward questions, ruled-out directions, and Next Focus.\n    30\t- **Mutability:** Mutable — analyst-owned sections remain stable, while machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration. Section 3 is a generated projection from the reducer registry.\n    31\t- **Protection:** Shared state with explicit ownership boundaries. Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n    32\t\n    33\t### Question Injection Surface\n    34\t\n    35\tUse `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl` to append external questions during an active run. Each line is one JSON object with:\n    36\t\n    37\t- `id`: stable inbox record identifier\n    38\t- `text`: question text to promote\n    39\t- `source`: concrete source label, such as an angle bank entry, analyst strategy, or operator note\n    40\t- `origin`: one of `angle-bank`, `analyst-strategy`, `operator`, or `legacy-import`\n    41\t- `injectedAtIteration`: iteration number when the question was introduced\n    42\t- `promotedQuestionId`: promoted registry question id, or `null` until promotion\n    43\t\n    44\tThe reducer reads the inbox on every reduce step and carries `origin` into the question registry and dashboard badges. Direct edits to Section 3 still work as a compatibility path, but they are attributed as `legacy-import`.\n    45\t\n    46\tQuestion ownership is explicit:\n    47\t\n    48\t- Inbox rows are immutable input.\n    49\t- The reducer registry is canonical question state.\n    50\t- Section 3 is rendered only from the registry view.\n    51\t\n    52\tWhen an inbox row targets an existing registry question but carries different text, the reducer keeps the registry value, records `operatorDecision: needs_decision`, and appends a `question_conflict` event with both `inboxValue` and `registryValue`.\n    53\t\n    54\t---\n    55\t\n    56\t## 2. TOPIC\n    57\t[Research topic from config -- set during initialization]\n    58\t\n    59\t---\n    60\t\n    61\t<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n    62\t## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n    63\tGenerated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`; direct edits are imported as compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\n    64\t\n    65\t- [ ] [Question 1 -- identified during initialization or iteration 1]\n    66\t- [ ] [Question 2]\n    67\t- [ ] [Question 3]\n    68\t<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n    69\t\n    70\t---\n    71\t\n    72\t## 4. NON-GOALS\n    73\t[What this research session is NOT trying to answer -- populated during initialization]\n    74\t\n    75\t---\n    76\t\n    77\t## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n    78\t[Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n    79\t\n    80\t---\n    81\t\n    82\t<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n    83\t## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n    84\t[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n    85\t<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n    86\t\n    87\t---\n    88\t\n    89\t<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n    90\t<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n    91\t## 7. WHAT WORKED\n    92\t[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n    93\t- [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n    94\t<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n    95\t\n    96\t---\n    97\t\n    98\t<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n    99\t## 8. WHAT FAILED\n   100\t[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n   101\t- [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n   102\t<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n   103\t\n   104\t---\n   105\t\n   106\t<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n   107\t## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n   108\t[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n   109\t\n   110\t### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n   111\t- What was tried: [specific approaches attempted]\n   112\t- Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n   113\t- Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n   114\t\n   115\t### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n   116\t- What worked: [successful approaches in this category]\n   117\t- Prefer for: [related questions where this category may help]\n   118\t<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n   119\t\n   120\t---\n   121\t\n   122\t<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n   123\t## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n   124\t[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n   125\t- [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n   126\t<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n   127\t\n   128\t---\n   129\t\n   130\t<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n   131\t## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n   132\t- Completed pivots: 0\n   133\t- Failed pivots: 0\n   134\t- Audited overrides: 0\n   135\t- Saturated: none yet\n   136\t- Pivot lineage: none yet\n   137\t- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n   138\t<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n   139\t\n   140\t---\n   141\t\n   142\t<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n   143\t## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n   144\t[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n   145\t<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n   146\t\n   147\t---\n   148\t\n   149\t<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n   150\t## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n   151\t[Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration]\n   152\t<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n   153\t\n   154\t---\n   155\t\n   156\t<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n   157\t## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n   158\t[Populated during initialization from the continuity ladder and ripgrep recipes, if any prior work exists]\n   159\t\n   160\t### Bounded Context Snapshot\n   161\t\n   162\tPopulate during initialization when the target is codebase-scoped. Keep this pointer-based and small:\n   163\t\n   164\t- Source pointers: paths, symbols, or resource-map entries relevant to the topic.\n   165\t- Reuse candidates: existing utilities, patterns, docs, or agents worth extending.\n   166\t- Integration points: files or contracts the research is likely to touch.\n   167\t- Constraints and risks: scope limits, stale graph or memory gaps, and known non-goals.\n   168\t\n   169\tDo not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use `@context` for one-shot retrieval, and use this snapshot only to seed the research loop.\n   170\t\n   171\t---\n   172\t\n   173\t## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n   174\t- Max iterations: [from config]\n   175\t- Convergence threshold: [from config]\n   176\t- Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n   177\t- Progressive synthesis: true (default)\n   178\t- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n   179\t- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\n   180\t- Machine-owned secti","truncated":true}
