{"type":"thinking","text":"No explicit 17-section list exists beyond names. I'll use a sensible canonical 17-section research report structure consistent with the references (Exec Summary, Background, Scope/Method, Findings sections..., Recommendations, Eliminated Alternatives, Divergence Map, Open Questions, References, Convergence Report). Since this is a research lineage, exhaustive template fidelity isn't the core criterion; the synthesis docs need to exist and be correct.\n\nNow, an important thing: the deep-research task itself is NOT the Phase 13 objective. The research_topic for this lineage is the specific question about the two route patches. The lineage completion is about producing the research output. The completion criteria in the prompt's \"Goal\" block apply to the parent packet, not necessarily this lineage. But wait — the durable directive and completion criteria describe the whole Phase 13. Hmm, this session is a dispatched fan-out lineage with research_topic: \"What do the two checked-in DeepSeek Harness route patches under .dsh/patches/ declare (endpoint, model id, reasoning effort, compat flags), and do they agree with each other? Read the files; answer in under 200 words.\"\n\nSo my job: run the deep-research workflow for that topic, maxIterations 1, and produce the lineage artifacts. The final answer must be the FANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE line. The completion criteria about evidence/ etc. are the parent packet's; my lineage should feed it. I should focus on the research topic.\n\nLet me now check the config's expected fields for the gateway run opening. step_create_state_log reads config topic and lineage.sessionId. So config must have lineage.sessionId and topic, specFolder, maxIterations, antiConvergence.convergenceMode. Let me create config with:\n- topic\n- maxIterations: 1\n- minIterations: 3 (workflow says populate 3) — but effective min clamps to max=1, so fine. Actually reducer might use minIterations; use 1 to be safe? The workflow populates 3 always. With maxIterations 1, effective_min_iterations = 1. I'll put minIterations: 1? Hmm, \"populate minIterations: 3\" is the workflow. But the fanout runner config probably writes config with maxIterations=1 and minIterations maybe 1. I'll follow workflow literally with minIterations: 3, since the check clamps to maxIterations. But the loop step compares iteration_count >= max_iterations first → STOP maxIterationsReached. Good.\n- convergenceThreshold: default 0.05 (not given in prompt; config.stopPolicy: convergence). The fanout run passes --convergence-threshold default 0.05, --stop-policy convergence, --convergence-mode default. So use 0.05.\n- stopPolicy: convergence\n- antiConvergence: {minIterations: 3, convergenceMode: \"default\"}. The workflow sets antiConvergence.stopPolicy from stop_policy too. Template has antiConvergence.stopPolicy: \"fail-closed\". I'll set stopPolicy: \"convergence\".\n- stuckThreshold: 3, maxDurationMinutes: 120\n- progressiveSynthesis: true\n- specFolder\n- createdAt ISO now\n- status initialized\n- executionMode auto\n- executor: {kind: \"cli-deepseek-harness\", model: \"deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017\", reasoningEffort: \"max\", serviceTier: null, sandboxMode: \"workspace-write\", permissionMode: \"workspace-write\", timeoutSeconds: 900} — should reflect invocation metadata? The fanout runner likely expects executor config. The prompt says executor: cli-deepseek-harness model=deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017. I can include those fields. The gateway's run_initialized computes executorFingerprint from config.executor. Fine.\n- lineage: sessionId \"fanout-dsh-live-2-1793981140452-hfbn1g\", parentSessionId null, lineageMode \"new\", generation 1, continuedFromRun null, allowedModes/deferredModes.\n- reducer, capabilityMatrixPath etc. like template.\n- resource_map_present: false, resource_map: {emit: true}\n- nextRunAt null, remainingDelayMs null\n\nSession ID: fanout-dsh-live-2-1793981140452-hfbn1g.\n\nNow, strategy key questions (3-5). For this topic:\n1. What endpoint and model id does route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml declare?\n2. What endpoint and model id does route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml declare?\n3. Which reasoning effort and compat flags does each patch declare?\n4. Where do the two patches disagree (endpoint, model id, compat, default selection)?\n\nThese need to be clear and match answeredQuestions text exactly if I tick them. I will answer all 4, so answeredQuestions should list exact texts.\n\nBut wait, the reducer ticks boxes only on exact match. Let me use these exact strings in strategy:\n- \"What endpoint and model id does route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml declare?\"\n- \"What endpoint and model id does route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml declare?\"\n- \"What reasoning effort and compat flags does each route patch declare?\"\n- \"Where do the two route patches disagree with each other?\"\n\nNow the research itself: I've read the two patches. The question asks specifically about \"the two checked-in DeepSeek Harness route patches\" — this is route-llmgateway-deepseek and route-opencode-go-deepseek. I should read them more carefully for line-level citations. Already have:\n\nroute-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml:\n- line 1-2 comment: Pins dispatch to LLM Gateway's DeepSeek V4.1 Flash instead of the base default route.\n- id llm-pi-ai, provider llmgateway, displayName LLM Gateway, apiKeyEnv LLMGATEWAY_API_KEY, api openai-completions, baseURL https://api.llmgateway.io/v1\n- compat.thinkingFormat: deepseek; compat.supportsDeveloperRole: false\n- model id: deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017, name DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\n- reasoningEfforts: off: (empty), high: high, max: max\n- agent-default-model: provider llmgateway, model deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017, reasoningEffort max\n\nroute-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml:\n- comment: Pins dispatch to OpenCode Go's DeepSeek V4.1 Flash instead of the base default; the endpoint is unverified until a keyed run proves it.\n- provider opencode-go, displayName OpenCode Go, apiKeyEnv OPENCODE_API_KEY, api openai-completions, baseURL https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1\n- compat.thinkingFormat deepseek; supportsDeveloperRole false\n- model id: deepseek-v4.1-flash (no -1017 suffix), name DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\n- reasoningEfforts: off/high/max same\n- agent-default-model: provider opencode-go, model deepseek-v4.1-flash, reasoningEffort max\n\nAgreement: they agree on api type (openai-completions), compat flags (thinkingFormat=deepseek, supportsDeveloperRole=false), reasoning effort ladder (off/high/max) and default selection at max; disagree on provider id/display name, API key env var, baseURL, and model id (pinned -1017 snapshot vs floating alias). Also one is declared verified? The opencode comment says endpoint unverified until a keyed run proves it. The LLM Gateway comment says \"Pins dispatch ... instead of the base default route\" — no verification note.\n\nI should also gather supporting evidence from the packet docs about routes, e.g., 013 packet docs or cli-deepseek-harness SKILL.md, to cross-check what the routes are supposed to be. The research topic says \"Read the files; answer in under 200 words\" — the two patch files are primary. For source diversity, I can add a second source: maybe the cli-deepseek-harness SKILL.md route roster, or the 013 spec/evidence. Let me look at the packet's docs for route descriptions. Let me search for \"opencode-go\" and \"llmgateway\" in the spec folder and skills.\n\nAlso check the containment baseline copies? `containment/baseline/.dsh/README.md` etc. Not relevant.\n\nLet me grep."}
