n't ours.\n\nActually wait: the dispatch prompt says \"After each iteration's gateway append, run the workflow's step_reduce_state reducer exactly as the YAML runs it: node ... reduce-state.cjs <spec_folder> --artifact-dir <lineage>\". The YAML's reducer command is `node ... reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg}` where reducer_artifact_arg = \"--artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\" for fanout. So exactly: `node ... reduce-state.cjs specs/... --artifact-dir specs/.../lineages/dsh-live-2`. Great.\n\nFor synthesis: run `node ... reduce-state.cjs <spec_folder> --artifact-dir <lineage> --emit-resource-map` (the non-fanout branch command with the artifact-dir arg added — the YAML's `if_absent` command is `... --emit-resource-map`, and reducer_artifact_arg is not used in that step. Hmm, the YAML's step_emit_resource_map command doesn't include {reducer_artifact_arg}. For a lineage override, without --artifact-dir the reducer would try resolveArtifactRoot(spec_folder, research) and find the root research dir. But we must write only inside lineage, so we can't let it write to the root research dir. The safest interpretation: include --artifact-dir to bind to lineage (the step_resolve_artifact_root binds artifact_dir; the command uses {spec_folder} but resource map needs lineage). The fanout branch's `--fanout-resource-map-only` without artifact-dir also seems odd; likely fanout-run.cjs orchestrates the root merge. Since I'm the lineage, use --artifact-dir.\n\nAlso phase_synthesis step_convergence_report uses synthesis-closeout.cjs with --artifact-dir {state_paths.packet_dir} = lineage, --state-log lineage/deep-research-state.jsonl, --registry, --output, --dashboard. Then it writes event files to event dir and gateway appends. It probably appends synthesis_complete and synthesis_incomplete rows. But note: PINNED_LEGACY_EVENTS includes synthesis_complete/synthesis_incomplete → the workflow's state_write_protocol says pinned bookkeeping events are recorded through book