ine 17. Fine. I read lines 1-70; the line numbers from the output: line 1 `---`, etc. Let me count: The README content printed, but I don't have cat -n. The sibling cites README:17 and README:28. Their line numbers likely correct. To be safe, I can grep -n for those sentences. Let me verify exact line numbers with grep before writing citations. Similarly SYNC line 25, and dump-config line numbers.\n\nLet me run a quick grep -n for exact anchors."}
