{"type":"tool_result","callId":"call_00_lTxcmLYcvVjBF4ENAzUg8236","status":"completed","result":"=== patch LLM ===\n2:- id: llm-pi-ai\n5:      llmgateway:\n7:        apiKeyEnv: LLMGATEWAY_API_KEY\n9:        baseURL: https://api.llmgateway.io/v1\n11:          thinkingFormat: deepseek\n12:          supportsDeveloperRole: false\n14:          - id: deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017\n20:- id: agent-default-model\n24:    reasoningEffort: max\n=== patch OC ===\n2:# the endpoint is unverified until a keyed run proves it.\n3:- id: llm-pi-ai\n6:      opencode-go:\n8:        apiKeyEnv: OPENCODE_API_KEY\n10:        baseURL: https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1\n12:          thinkingFormat: deepseek\n13:          supportsDeveloperRole: false\n21:- id: agent-default-model\n25:    reasoningEffort: max\n=== README ===\n17:`dsh` reads this folder only when a dispatch names its files with `--patch`. A dispatch passes exactly one route patch, the lineage patch and the guards patch. The route patch picks the provider and model. The lineage patch turns off telemetry export, the DeepSeek session log, goal rounds and plan mode.\n28:| `patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml` | Routes to OpenCode Go, model `deepseek-v4.1-flash`, key variable `OPENCODE_API_KEY`. Endpoint unverified |\n=== SYNC ===\n3:description: \"How .dsh derives from .skilled: hand-authored route and lineage patches, a generated skill-link farm, prompt stubs and persona patches, and what this folder never holds.\"\n24:| `patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml` | **hand-authored** route patch | none | Yes. `--dump-config` shows the composed `llm-pi-ai` provider and the `agent-default-model` row |\n25:| `patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml` | **hand-authored** route patch | none | Yes, same check. Its endpoint is unverified until a keyed run proves it |\n26:| `patches/lineage.patch.yml` | **hand-authored** lineage patch | none | Yes. `--dump-config` shows telemetry `DISABLED` and the four disabled rows |\n27:| `patches/guards.patch.yml` | **hand-authored** patch that inserts the `repo-guards` row | none | Yes. A keyless boot with it must print no `did not activate` line |\n28:| `patches/mcp-code-mode.patch.yml` | **hand-authored**, opt-in patch that mounts one `code_mode` stdio server | `.pi/mcp.json` | Yes. A keyless boot with it must leave no new `mcp-code-mode-launcher` process |\n29:| `plugins/repo-guards/` | **hand-authored** plugin bundle; its adapters call the shared guard cores under `.skilled/` | `.skilled/hooks/`, `.skilled/skills/*/runtime/hooks/` | Yes. `node --test .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/tests/` |\n33:| `README.md` | hand-authored | none | No |\n34:| `SYNC.md` | hand-authored | none | No |\n66:The two route patches replace two rows. `llm-pi-ai` gets one custom provider with `apiKeyEnv` naming the key variable, never a key value. `agent-default-model` gets that provider, its single model and the default effort `max`. Each provider carries `compat.thinkingFormat: deepseek`, so `off` sends `thinking: {type: disabled}`, and `compat.supportsDeveloperRole: false`, because the gateway upstream refuses the `developer` role. Each model declares `off`, `high` and `max`, since a hand-declared model has no reasoning levels until the patch declares them. Whether either endpoint accepts `max` on the wire is unverified until a keyed run.\n=== dumps ===\nspecs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/evidence/dump-config-llmgateway.txt:60:    provider: llmgateway\nspecs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/evidence/dump-config-llmgateway.txt:61:    model: deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017\nspecs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/evidence/dump-config-llmgateway.txt:62:    reasoningEffort: max\nspecs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/evidence/dump-config-opencode-go.txt:60:    provider: opencode-go\nspecs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/evidence/dump-config-opencode-go.txt:61:    model: deepseek-v4.1-flash\nspecs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/evidence/dump-config-opencode-go.txt:62:    reasoningEffort: max\n"}
