{"type":"thinking","text":"Great. Now I need the exact model id line for OC: grep with `$` didn't match because `- id: deepseek-v4.1-flash` has leading spaces; my pattern anchored end okay? It printed no line for OC model. Let me check line 15: from cat -n earlier: line 15 `          - id: deepseek-v4.1-flash`. The grep pattern `id: deepseek-v4.1-flash$` should match... unless there's trailing whitespace. It's line 15. I'll cite line 15. For LLM line 14 verified.\n\nAlso effort ladder lines: LLM 16-19; OC 17-20. Compat: LLM 11-12; OC 12-13.\n\nNow write the iteration narrative. Keep it thorough and accurate. Findings count = 5. newInfoRatio 1.0 (all new). Status complete. answeredQuestions = all 4 key questions exactly as in strategy:\n- \"What endpoint and model id does `.dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml` declare?\"\n- \"What endpoint and model id does `.dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml` declare?\"\n- \"What reasoning effort and compat flags does each route patch declare?\"\n- \"Where do the two route patches disagree with each other?\"\n\nNote: the reducer determines resolved questions by matching answeredQuestions text to registry questions (exact). Good.\n\nIteration record fields:\n{\n\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"run\":1,\"runId\":\"...\",\"sessionId\":\"...\",\"lineageId\":\"...\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Read the two DSH route patches and compare their declarations.\",\"findingsCount\":5,\"newInfoRatio\":1,\"noveltyJustification\":\"All five findings are new to this lineage, which had no prior research state.\",\"keyQuestions\":[...4...],\"answeredQuestions\":[...4...],\"ruledOut\":[],\"edgeCase\":\"none\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[...],\"timestamp\":\"<now>\",\"durationMs\":...,\"executor\":{...}\n}\n\ndurationMs: from init 16:08:45 to now ~16:10. Let me get current time and compute a plausible duration. The research actions have been ongoing since 16:05 dispatch. I'll use the actual elapsed from config createdAt to iteration timestamp. Get time now.\n\n`edgeCase`: \"none\" (no ambiguous input etc.). There is a scope conflict (spec.md writeback skipped) — recorded in narrative Edge Cases as \"Scope conflicts\". Should edgeCase be \"partial-success\"? The workflow says edgeCase is one of none, ambiguous-input, contradictory-evidence, missing-dependency, partial-success. The research itself is complete; the workflow-level scope skip is not a research edge case. Use \"none\".\n\nAlso should I include graphEvents? The prompt pack says optional. I could add coverage graph nodes/edges to be richer: nodes for the two source files and findings, edges CITES/SUPPORTS. But the reducer's graph upsert runs later (not in my synthesis). The convergence graph is empty anyway. Optional; I'll skip to keep the record clean. Actually, adding graphEvents could enrich the dashboard; the workflow's reducer handles graphEvents from the delta. But graph convergence evaluation is skipped. I'll include a small graph: nodes for QUESTION (4), FINDING (5), SOURCE (2), and edges ANSWERS/SUPPORTS/CITES. This is optional and risks schema errors; the prompt pack documents exact shapes. It could help the \"clean containment\" but not needed. Given max 1 iteration and the ask is a reading answer, skip graphEvents. The sibling didn't include them.\n\nNow the delta file: iteration row + 5 finding rows with label and sources. The finding rows' label text should be the finding statement; sources array lists repo-relative paths. The reducer may use the iteration narrative for registry keyFindings (as observed) — it actually used the narrative text with citations. To be safe, make the finding labels match the narrative findings (maybe without the full citation tags? The sibling's labels were shorter than narrative, yet registry used narrative text. Either way, closeout compares registry keys derived from finding identities; it should pass as long as registry keyFindings count >= identifiable findings. The reducer builds keyFindings from narrative findings, it seems. Let me not worry.)\n\nDelta finding rows:\n1. id f-iter001-001, label: \"`route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml` declares provider `llmgateway`, baseURL `https://api.llmgateway.io/v1`, api `openai-completions`, key `LLMGATEWAY_API_KEY`, model `deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`, default effort `max`.\" sources: [\".dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml\"]\n2. f-iter001-002 OC declarations.\n3. f-iter001-003 agree on compat and effort ladder.\n4. f-iter001-004 disagree on provider/endpoint/key/model; OC endpoint unverified.\n5. f-iter001-005 alternative pins, not additive; dump-config corroborates.\n\nSources arrays should include the actual paths (no backticks in paths). The guidance says repo-relative file path. Use plain paths.\n\nNow write iteration narrative + delta + gateway event file. I'll use the write tool for the narrative, and write the delta/event via write tool too (JSONL content). Then gateway.\n\nTime check first."}
