{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_u25kanmwhodYsh2lG8Cl1119","tool":"write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/013-dsh-live-contract-pin/research/fanout-live-2/lineages/dsh-live-2/iterations/iteration-001.md","content":"# Iteration 1: DSH route patch declarations\n\n## Focus\n\nRead the two checked-in DeepSeek Harness route patches under `.dsh/patches/`, record the endpoint, model id, reasoning effort and compat flags each declares, and compare them. The topic asks for a reading answer under 200 words; no keyed probe or dispatch is in scope.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read `.dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml` lines 1-24.\n2. Read `.dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml` lines 1-25.\n3. Read `.dsh/README.md` lines 1-53 and `.dsh/SYNC.md` lines 1-66 for the route inventory and verification labels.\n4. Read the prior 004 packet's `--dump-config` evidence for each route to corroborate the composed provider, model and default effort.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. `route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml` declares provider `llmgateway` at `https://api.llmgateway.io/v1` with `api: openai-completions`, `apiKeyEnv: LLMGATEWAY_API_KEY`, model id `deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`, and default `reasoningEffort: max`. [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml:5] [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml:9] [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml:14] [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml:24]\n2. `route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml` declares provider `opencode-go` at `https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1` with `api: openai-completions`, `apiKeyEnv: OPENCODE_API_KEY`, model id `deepseek-v4.1-flash`, and default `reasoningEffort: max`. [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml:6] [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml:10] [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml:15] [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml:25]\n3. Both patches declare the same compat block, `thinkingFormat: deepseek` and `supportsDeveloperRole: false`, and the same effort ladder `off` / `high: high` / `max: max` with `max` selected by default. [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml:11] [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml:12] [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml:16] [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml:12] [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml:13] [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml:17]\n4. They disagree on provider id, endpoint, key variable, and exact model id (`deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017` vs `deepseek-v4.1-flash`); the OpenCode Go patch itself says its endpoint is \"unverified until a keyed run proves it\". [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml:1] [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml:2] [SOURCE: .dsh/README.md:28]\n5. The two are alternative pins, not additive: both target the same `llm-pi-ai` and `agent-default-model` rows, and the repository says a dispatch passes exactly one route patch. Prior `--dump-config` evidence shows each patch composing its own provider and model separately. [SOURCE: .dsh/README.md:17] [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/evidence/dump-config-llmgateway.txt:60] [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/evidence/dump-config-opencode-go.txt:60]\n\n## Questions Answered\n\n- What endpoint and model id does `.dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml` declare?\n- What endpoint and model id does `.dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml` declare?\n- What reasoning effort and compat flags does each route patch declare?\n- Where do the two route patches disagree with each other?\n\n## Questions Remaining\n\nNone for the stated reading scope. Endpoint health and keyed dispatch are explicitly out of scope.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\nNone. The direct-file reading path answered every in-scope question in one pass.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\nNone.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: none. \"Agree\" is read as agreement in the declared fields, not as runtime equivalence.\n- Contradictory evidence: none. The patches and the repository docs agree on the values; the two patches differ by design, and the OpenCode Go comment states the verification gap explicitly.\n- Missing dependencies: no keyed execution evidence exists in this lineage, so endpoint health is recorded as unverified rather than inferred. This is the documented state, not a failure.\n- Partial success: none. All four key questions are answered from checked-in files.\n- Scope conflicts: the auto-workflow's `step_graph_convergence` and post-synthesis `spec.md` writeback were not performed because they resolve outside this lineage's write surface; the terminal `maxIterationsReached` cap bypasses the graph gate. The final synthesis and save steps that remain in scope are recorded in the synthesis section.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml`\n- `.dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml`\n- `.dsh/README.md`\n- `.dsh/SYNC.md`\n- `specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/evidence/dump-config-llmgateway.txt`\n- `specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/evidence/dump-config-opencode-go.txt`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 1.0\n- Novelty justification: all five findings are new to this lineage, which had no prior research state.\n- Questions addressed: all four key questions.\n- Questions answered: all four key questions.\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: reading the two patch files directly, then checking the repository's own route inventory and the prior `--dump-config` evidence, produced a declaration-level answer with three independent corroborations and no need for a keyed run.\n- What did not work and why: nothing failed. The only unavailable input is a keyed dispatch, which the topic does not request and the frozen scope excludes.\n- What I would do differently: nothing for a one-iteration reading task; a keyed run would be a separate verification phase, not a deeper read.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nNone: `config.maxIterations` is 1. If the parent needs endpoint health, a keyed dispatch under a fresh `DSH_HOME` is the next evidence step, and it is outside this lineage's scope.\n"}}
