anout absent), step_hydrate_summary_metrics, step_read_all_iterations, step_emit_resource_map, step_compile_research, step_convergence_report. The convergence report is generated by closeout? Wait, the YAML's step_convergence_report runs synthesis-closeout, but the \"report\" text is a separate field that is supposed to be appended to research.md. Looking at the YAML: step_convergence_report has `report: |` (the report content) and `command: |` (closeout + gateway). The closeout script does NOT append the report to research.md; it only validates and stages synthesis events. Hmm, does something else append the report? The step's report is a template; the workflow executor is expected to append it to research.md. The sibling's research.md has \"## 13. Convergence Report\" with the values, so the executor wrote it. I'll include the convergence report in research.md myself, before running closeout (closeout just requires the file).\n\nAlso the 17-section template: I'll structure research.md with:\n- Frontmatter\n- Title\n- ## Answer (under 200 words) — the requested answer\n- 1. Research Question\n- 2. Scope and Method\n- 3. Declarations (table)\n- 4. Agreement\n- 5. Differences\n- 6. Verification Status\n- 7. Evidence\n- 8. Implications\n- 9. Limitations\n- 10. Recommendations\n- 11. References\n- ## Eliminated Alternatives\n- ## Divergence Map\n- 12. Open Questions\n- 13. Convergence Report\n\nThat's 13 numbered sections + answer + mandated extra sections; \"17-section\" doesn't have a fixed list anywhere I found. The sibling used the same. Good.\n\nThe Answer section must be under 200 words. Let me draft and count. Use the sibling's answer as a basis but rephrase/ensure accuracy. Count words roughly.\n\nDraft:\n\"Both patches are alternative pins on the same two rows, `llm-pi-ai` and `agent-default-model`, so they cannot be combined.\n\nThe LLM Gateway patch declares provider `llmgateway`, endpoint `https://api.llmgateway.io/v1`, `api: openai-completions`, key variable `LLMGATEWAY_API_KEY`, model id `deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`, and default `reasoningEffort: max`.\n\nThe OpenCode Go patch declares provider `opencode-go`, endpoint `https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1`, the same API, key variable `OPENCODE_API_KEY`, model id `deepseek-v4.1-flash`, and the same default effort.\n\nThey agree on the API shape, the `off`/`high`/`max` effort ladder with `max` selected, and compat flags `thinkingFormat: deepseek` and `supportsDeveloperRole: false`. They disagree on provider id, endpoint, key variable, and exact model id. The OpenCode Go patch itself says its endpoint is \"unverified until a keyed run proves it\"; the LLM Gateway patch carries no such caveat.\"\n\nWord count: Let me count later with wc. Under 200 likely (~130). Good.\n\nNow run resource map reducer."}
